# ChangeLog


Version 2.1 (2026-03-25)

- Fixed Emulation -> Display -> Fullscreen so it reliably enters fullscreen
    mode on macOS instead of reverting to a windowed resize path.

- Added a macOS fullscreen fallback path for FLTK builds where fullscreen()
    does not immediately resize to the active screen bounds.

- Fixed macOS menu instability and crashes when using menu items after moving
    the main window across desktop Spaces.

- Switched the macOS main menu integration to Fl_Sys_Menu_Bar and adjusted
    window layout calculations accordingly.

- Fixed startup crash caused by early system-menu synchronization by deferring
    menu sync until the main window is shown.

- Fixed Space-jumping behavior where display-size changes could move the app
    back to Desktop 1.

- Fixed Space-jumping behavior during model switching by reusing the existing
    top-level main window on macOS and recreating only the display widget.

- Fixed a Memory Editor close crash caused by double-deleting a popup menu
    widget that was already owned and destroyed by FLTK parent teardown.

- Hardened tool-window close handling on macOS by using FLTK deferred widget
    deletion in close callbacks instead of immediate destruction during event
    dispatch.

- Deferred macOS tool-window creation from menu callbacks to the next event
    loop tick to avoid FLTK menu reentrancy and system-menu registration races.

- Marked tool windows as non-modal on macOS so FLTK does not register them in
    the native Window-menu path that was triggering Cocoa-side crashes.

- Fixed Disassembler teardown crash by removing manual deletion of FLTK-owned
    editor child widgets and initializing related pointers defensively.

- Removed duplicated embedded Tools submenus from secondary FLTK tool windows
    on macOS and use the native main Tools menu for cross-window navigation.

- Fixed C++ warning in Flu_Tree_Browser by replacing memset on non-trivial
    RData with proper value initialization.

- Fixed macOS linker warning:
    "reducing alignment of section __DATA,__common from 0x8000 to 0x4000"
    by zero-initializing large globals in memory.c so they are emitted as
    regular zero-fill data definitions.


Version 2.0 (2026-03-22)

- Used #if LCD_DELAY_SIMULATION to block comment out the too agressive LCD
    display controller delay in io.c.

- Improved macOS keyboard handling for M100/M102/T200-family input by
    normalizing shifted punctuation from MacBook keyboards to the base key
    events expected by the emulator.

- Added normalization support for the following shifted punctuation keys on
    macOS: `:+"<>?_{}|~`.

- Added smart-quote normalization for macOS text input so Unicode quote
    variants map to the emulated quote key path instead of being dropped.


Version 1.9 (2026-03-21)

- Fixed crash when switching models (e.g., M100 to T200) caused by improper
    deletion of FLTK-managed menu widgets in T100_Disp destructor. The menu
    button widgets (m_LeftClick, m_LeftClickQuad, m_CopyCut) are managed by FLTK
    and should not be explicitly deleted. Changed destructor to only null out
    pointers instead of calling delete, allowing FLTK to handle cleanup properly.


Version 1.8 (2026-03-21)

- Fixed macOS C++ compile failure in preference handling by using C++-safe
    conversion (`std::atoi`) and proper header usage in `pref_form.cpp`.

- Fixed arm64 link failure in remote processing by replacing legacy
    `fl_wait(double)` usage with FLTK API `Fl::wait(...)` calls.

- Updated build/link flags for Darwin to remove stale/legacy library paths
    (including old X11 and Homebrew libpng path handling) and removed duplicate
    pthread linkage noise in makefiles.

- Performed project-wide `sprintf` to `snprintf` migration across modified
    source files to address modern macOS deprecation warnings.

- Updated FLTK API usage in editor/UI code to newer calls where needed
    (including replacement of deprecated cursor-position methods).

- Corrected memory-management and safety issues found during warning cleanup,
    including mismatched `new[]`/`delete` handling and related warning fixes.

- Resolved additional compiler warnings across C/C++ modules, including
    assignment-in-condition cleanup, prototype modernization, empty-body cleanup,
    logical precedence fixes, and unused/extra argument fixes.

- Added Apple-clang scoped suppression around deprecated `sem_init` usage in
    `m100emu.c` to keep build output clean while preserving behavior.

- Applied related formatting-safe warning cleanups in touched modules such as
    assembler/disassembler, IDE/editor windows, memory tools, socket dialogs,
    printer/paper views, and peripheral/remote support code.

- Verified successful full build after the above changes (`virtualt` and
    `vt_client` binaries produced).


For versions prior to Version 1.8, see [release.txt](./release.txt).
